.TH PORCUPIN-SERVER 1 "January 2026" "v0.3.2" "Porcupin Manual"
.SH NAME
porcupin-server \- Headless IPFS backup node for Tezos assets
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B porcupin-server
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B porcupin-server
is the headless daemon for the Porcupin application. It monitors configured Tezos wallets and automatically pins their associated NFT assets (images, metadata, videos) to an embedded IPFS node.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-config \fIpath\fR
Path to configuration file (default: ~/.porcupin/config.yaml).
.TP
.B \-data \fIpath\fR
Data directory for database and IPFS repo (default: ~/.porcupin).
.TP
.B \-update
Check for and install the latest version from GitHub.
.TP
.B \-serve
Start the API server for remote management.
.TP
.B \-api-port \fIport\fR
Port for the API server (default: 8085).
.TP
.B \-api-bind \fIaddress\fR
Bind address for the API server (default: 0.0.0.0).
.TP
.B \-list-wallets
List all tracked wallets and exit.
.TP
.B \-add-wallet \fIaddress\fR
Add a wallet address to track and exit.
.TP
.B \-remove-wallet \fIaddress\fR
Remove a wallet address (stop tracking) and exit.
.TP
.B \-version
Show version information and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.B Start the server in background:
.RS
porcupin-server --serve &
.RE
.PP
.B Update to latest version:
.RS
porcupin-server --update
.RE
.SH FILES
.I ~/.porcupin/config.yaml
.RS
Configuration file.
.RE
.I ~/.porcupin/porcupin.db
.RS
SQLite database.
.RE
.SH AUTHOR
Developed by skllzrmy.tez
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ipfs (1)
